"crichmon" <crichmon23@hotmail.com> writes:
> I'm curious to find out what NetHackers might think of this idea: a
> roguelike game that was 3D.  I don't necessarily mean Dungeon Siege or
> Ultima Underworld.  Merely an environment based on 3D cubes/rectangular
> prisms rather then the traditional 2D squares/rectangles that most
> roguelikes are based on (due to the ascii character set).  Is there anyone
> out there who would be interested in playing such a game?
> 
> I know this probably belongs on r.g.r.d, but I wanted some opinions from
> r.g.r.n posters as I am a long-time Hack/NetHack fan.

NetHack _is_ 3D. It just places severe constraints on movement along
the z axis.

(Seriously, there have been occasional discussions at London rgrns
about how you might implement a single dungeon level that's at
multiple elevations. In general, though, I don't think there's much
you can _do_ with vertical distance, unless you're thinking of
implementing aerial dogfights between flying creatures in a huge
cavern or something; I doubt the gains would be worth the
implementation hassle.)

